{"@context":"http://iiif.io/api/presentation/3/context.json","id":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grecolatinovivo-create/emendando-catalogo/manifesti/data/manifesti/romani-pas/409249.json","type":"Manifest","label":{"none":["PAS LIN-D92A22: Early Medieval lead spindle whorl with Norse runes"]},"metadata":[{"label":{"it":["Oggetto"]},"value":{"none":["fusarola"]}},{"label":{"it":["Supporto"]},"value":{"none":["piombo (fusarola)"]}},{"label":{"it":["Datazione"]},"value":{"none":["1000-1100 d.C."]}},{"label":{"it":["Provenienza"]},"value":{"none":["contea di ritrovamento: Lincolnshire (Inghilterra e Galles)"]}},{"label":{"it":["Descrizione"]},"value":{"none":["An inscribed lead spindle dating to the early 11th century. The whorl is trapezoid in cross-section and roughly circular in plan. An hour-glass shaped hole has been drilled through the centre, measuring circa 8mm diameter at the opening. The whorl is inscribed on the side and base with Norse runes. Dr. John Hines (Cardiff University) has examined the whorl. He writes: In late summer of 2010 a…"]}},{"label":{"it":["Identificativo PAS"]},"value":{"none":["LIN-D92A22"]}},{"label":{"it":["FindID"]},"value":{"none":["409249"]}}],"requiredStatement":{"label":{"it":["Attribuzione"]},"value":{"it":["Portable Antiquities Scheme / The Trustees of the British Museum (Portable Antiquities Scheme, finds.org.uk). Foto: Lincolnshire County Council, Adam Daubney, 2011-04-27 11:43:56, CC BY-SA 2.0 ; Lincolnshire County Council, Adam Daubney, 2011-04-27 11:43:56, CC BY-SA 4.0, da Wikimedia Commons. Manifesto scritto da Emendando."]}},"homepage":[{"id":"https://finds.org.uk/database/artefacts/record/id/409249","type":"Text","label":{"none":["PAS LIN-D92A22: Early Medieval lead spindle whorl with Norse runes"]},"format":"text/html"}],"items":[{"id":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/grecolatinovivo-create/emendando-catalogo/manifesti/data/manifesti/romani-pas/409249.json/canvas/1","type":"Canvas","label":{"none":["Lincolnshire Co